       <!-- TAB 2: GRAMMAR -->
        <div id="grammar" class="tab-content">
            <div class="card-grid">
                <div class="info-card">
                    <h3>Syntax & Word Order</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>SVO:</strong> Subject – Verb – Object.</li>
                        <li><strong>Simple vs. Composed Subject:</strong> Simple written as-is; composed/modified subjects hyphenated (e.g., <em>Ta’ haskto na-eira</em> vs <em>Ta’ haskto na eira</em>).</li>
                        <li><strong>Interrogation:</strong> <code>ka-</code> prefix + subject + verb.</li>
                        <li><strong>Negative:</strong> <code>ne-</code> prefix before the word.</li>
                        <li><strong>Comparison:</strong> Prefix <code>'shta</code>.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="info-card">
                    <h3>Semantics & Tone</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Harsh sounds:</strong> Raw feelings (grief, anger), war, day-to-day, political contexts.</li>
                        <li><strong>Soft sounds:</strong> Intimate, soulful, hope, love, sacred/ritualistic (masses, preaching).</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="info-card">
                    <h3>Adjective Placement</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Harsh tone:</strong> Subject then adjective (unpolished, e.g., <em>eira na</em>).</li>
                        <li><strong>Soft tone:</strong> Adjective then subject (poetic/polished, e.g., <em>na eira</em>).</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="info-card">
                    <h3>Verb Conjugation</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Present:</strong> No change to the word whatsoever.</li>
                        <li><strong>Infinitive:</strong> Base + <code>-ar</code>.</li>
                        <li><strong>Past:</strong> <code>ha-</code> prefix.</li>
                        <li><strong>Future:</strong> <code>vi-</code> prefix.</li>
                        <li><strong>Conditional:</strong> <code>lo-</code> prefix.</li>
                        <li><strong>Imperative:</strong> Drop subject.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- TAB 3: GENDERS & PRONOUNS -->
        <div id="genders" class="tab-content">
            <div class="card-grid">
                <div class="info-card">
                    <h3>Gendered Endings</h3>
                    <p><strong>Singular:</strong> Masc <code>-y</code> (boy – <em>lumay</em>), Fem <code>-ï</code> (girl – <em>lumaï</em>), Neut <code>-e</code> (child – <em>lumae</em>)</p>
                    <p><strong>Plural:</strong> Masc <code>-ey</code>, Fem <code>-it</code>, Neut <code>-eni</code></p>
                </div>
                <div class="info-card">
                    <h3>Personal Pronouns</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li>I/Me – <em>Aen</em> | You – <em>A’bi</em> | He/she/it – <em>Y’le</em></li>
                        <li>We – <em>E’tan</em> | You (pl.) – <em>A’bie</em> | They – <em>Y’ma</em></li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="info-card">
                    <h3>Possessive Pronouns</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Mine – <em>Aeni</em> | Your – <em>Abi’ri</em> | His/Hers/Its – <em>Yle’ri</em></li>
                        <li>Our – <em>Etan’ri</em> | Yours (pl.) – <em>Abi’ma</em> | Theirs – <em>Yma’ri</em> | My – <em>Ae</em></li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

